  lore:
  - id: last-light/0
    title: Night shift
    company: AEGIS SYSTEMS
    contract: Last Light
    text: 'AEGIS / NIGHT OPERATIONS: Operators are instructed to treat missing telemetry as hostile activity. A handwritten note underneath reads: Some people simply turn off their phones. That is still allowed.'
  - id: last-light/1
    title: The targeting index
    company: AEGIS SYSTEMS
    contract: Last Light
    text: 'Index schema commentary: Risk scores include association with public-interest researchers, debt appeals, and community infrastructure. The system was never looking for a crime. It was looking for connections.'
  - id: last-light/2
    title: After the signal
    company: AEGIS SYSTEMS
    contract: Last Light
    text: 'Buffered message from NULL: When the index goes quiet, leave the relays running. People will need those connections tomorrow. We can build something better on the wires they left behind.'
